### Testing suricata configurations

suricata -T -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml -v

### Loading the default suricata configuration setup
suricata -T -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml -S /etc/suricata/rules/local.rules -v 

### you can reload rules but that's if you wish for that to happen

suricatac -c reload-rules

### Run a proper PCAP replay test

suricata -r /path/to/captured.pcap -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

### Note : in your suricata rules book you should have the following so suricata can pin point errors and logs

alert http any any -> any any (msg:"ATTACKER Curl Activity Detected"; http.user_agent; content:"curl"; sid:1000002; rev:1;)
